<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Gemex to pay dividend.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Gemex to pay dividend.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican bottling company Grupo Embotellador de Mexico SA said on Thursday it will set aside 79.20 million pesos for a dividend payment.</p>
<p>The company, PepsiCo Inc's anchor bottler in Mexico, said through the Mexican Stock Exchange that the dividend must be paid before May 31. It said the money for dividends would come from 1996 profits.</p>
<p>The company also said that shareholders in a recent assembly voted to keep 100 million pesos in a reserve to potentially repurchase company shares.</p>
<p>-- Karina Balderas, Mexico City newsroom 525 728-9562</p>
</text>
